    The proposed gate combines geometry, focus, exposure, and temporal stability Text boxes are detected in each video frame and merged into a candidate region The outer region must remain inside a safety margin so no line is cropped Its width and height must also fall within practical limits a tiny region provides too few pixels per character, but a region touching the image boundary probably indicates that part of the page is missing Focus is estimated from Laplacian variance over the ful grayscale frame. A second measurement covers the upper thirty percent. where slanted paper is commonly out of focus A capture is rejected when the upper score is much lower than the full-frame score, even if the overall number appears satisfactory
  P3 | type=paragraph | 9 line(s) | confidence=0.990 | in the lower part of the page
    One sharp frame is not sufficient evidence The position and size of the text region must remain stable across four consecutive observations. With the selected video interval, this adds roughly eight tenths of a second after the page first appears ready The delay is short for the wearer but long enough for hand and head motion to settle Exposure changes are monitored during the same period if brightness is still drifting, the counter returns to zero When the page is too large, spoken guidance hold still or adjust distance
